# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inputs {#inputs}"
msgstr "Mga input {#inputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `mode` determines which parameters a run needs. For a description of every input parameter, see the [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/kipu-rimay#inputs).\n"
msgstr "Ang `mode` ang nagtatakda kung aling mga parameter ang kailangan ng isang run. Para sa paglalarawan ng bawat input parameter, tingnan ang [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/kipu-rimay#inputs).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Input files {#input-files}"
msgstr "Mga input file {#input-files}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload every file with `catalog.file_upload()` before you run the function.\n"
msgstr "I-upload ang bawat file gamit ang `catalog.file_upload()` bago mo patakbuhin ang function.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "An upload replaces any earlier file of the same name, even for a job that you submitted but that has not started yet. To run several jobs at the same time, give the files of each job their own names, for example `run1_x_train.csv` and `run2_x_train.csv`.\n"
msgstr "Pinapalitan ng isang upload ang anumang naunang file na may parehong pangalan, kahit para sa job na isinumite mo pero hindi pa nagsisimula. Para magpatakbo ng ilang job nang sabay-sabay, bigyan ng sariling pangalan ang mga file ng bawat job, halimbawa `run1_x_train.csv` at `run2_x_train.csv`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every file is a CSV file with a header row. Every column of a feature file is one feature, and every value must be numeric.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat file ay CSV file na may header row. Ang bawat column ng feature file ay isang feature, at dapat numeric ang bawat value.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`y_train` holds exactly one numeric column, with one label per row of `x_train`. Map categorical labels to numbers, for example good and bad to 1 and 0.\n"
msgstr "Ang `y_train` ay may eksaktong isang numeric na column, na may isang label bawat row ng `x_train`. I-map ang mga categorical label sa mga numero, halimbawa good at bad sa 1 at 0.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`x_test` and `x_inference` must have the same columns as `x_train`, in the same order.\n"
msgstr "Dapat magkapareho ang mga column ng `x_test` at `x_inference` at ng `x_train`, sa parehong ayos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Keep the mapping_id and backend_name\">\n"
"  The `mapping_id` is the only way to reach the mapping that your fit produced, and it cannot be looked up or recovered. It authorizes the use of that mapping, so treat it like a credential and do not share it. If you lose it, you must fit a new mapping, which costs another run on quantum hardware. Also record the `backend_name` of the fit, because the mapping runs only on that processor.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Itago ang mapping_id at backend_name\">\n"
"  Ang `mapping_id` ang tanging paraan para maabot ang mapping na nabuo ng iyong fit, at hindi ito mahahanap o mababawi. Pinapahintulutan nito ang paggamit ng mapping na iyon, kaya ituring itong credential at huwag ibahagi. Kung mawala mo ito, kailangan mong mag-fit ng bagong mapping, na nangangailangan ng isa pang run sa quantum hardware. Itala rin ang `backend_name` ng fit, dahil sa processor na iyon lang tumatakbo ang mapping.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Limits {#limits}"
msgstr "Mga limitasyon {#limits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every feature is mapped to one qubit, so the processor must have at least as many qubits as your data has features. If you have more features than that, reduce them with a feature selection technique first.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat feature ay imamapa sa isang qubit, kaya dapat may kahit kasing dami ng qubit ang processor kaysa sa bilang ng feature ng data mo. Kung mas marami ang feature mo, bawasan muna ang mga ito gamit ang feature selection technique.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every sample becomes one circuit, and a run counts training and test samples together. A run can hold at most 15,000 samples.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat sample ay nagiging isang circuit, at binibilang ng isang run ang training at test sample nang magkasama. Ang isang run ay maaaring maglaman ng hanggang 15,000 sample.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single job can request at most 10 million executions, so the number of samples times `shots` must not exceed 10 million.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang job ay maaaring humiling ng hanggang 10 milyong execution, kaya ang bilang ng mga sample na minultiply sa `shots` ay hindi dapat lumampas sa 10 milyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A job must finish within 24 hours, including the time its circuits wait in the processor's queue. A job that runs longer is stopped without a result. On a busy processor, keep large datasets well below these limits.\n"
msgstr "Dapat matapos ang isang job sa loob ng 24 oras, kasama ang oras na naghihintay ang mga circuit nito sa queue ng processor. Ang job na mas matagal tumakbo ay ihihinto nang walang resulta. Sa busy na processor, panatilihing mas mababa nang malayo sa mga limitasyong ito ang malalaking dataset.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Outputs {#outputs}"
msgstr "Mga output {#outputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` returns a dictionary. The quantum-transformed features themselves are written to CSV files that you download with `catalog.file_download()`. For a description of every key of the dictionary, see the [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/kipu-rimay#output). For the time that each execution phase took, see [Run metadata](#run-metadata).\n"
msgstr "Ang `job.result()` ay nagbabalik ng dictionary. Ang mga quantum-transformed feature mismo ay isinusulat sa mga CSV file na dina-download mo gamit ang `catalog.file_download()`. Para sa paglalarawan ng bawat key ng dictionary, tingnan ang [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/kipu-rimay#output). Para sa oras na inabot ng bawat execution phase, tingnan ang [Run metadata](#run-metadata).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every output file holds one row per input row, in the order of the input file, and one column per quantum-transformed feature. The columns whose names start with `corr_` are the two-body expectation values. The files hold no label column. The labels of your training data stay in your `y_train` file.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat output file ay may isang row bawat input row, sa ayos ng input file, at isang column bawat quantum-transformed feature. Ang mga column na ang pangalan ay nagsisimula sa `corr_` ay ang mga two-body expectation value. Walang label column ang mga file. Ang mga label ng training data mo ay nananatili sa iyong `y_train` file.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run metadata {#run-metadata}"
msgstr "Run metadata {#run-metadata}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`resource_usage` holds one entry for each execution phase that the run went through: `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`, `\"RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING\"`, and, on a QPU, usually `\"RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU\"`. Each entry holds `CPU_TIME`, the wall-clock time of the phase in seconds, and `QPU_TIME`, the QPU time in seconds. On a QPU, the QPU time that IBM billed is recorded under `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`, the phase in which the circuits ran.\n"
msgstr "Ang `resource_usage` ay may isang entry para sa bawat execution phase na dinaanan ng run: `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`, `\"RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING\"`, at, sa QPU, kadalasan `\"RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU\"`. Ang bawat entry ay may `CPU_TIME`, ang wall-clock time ng phase sa segundo, at `QPU_TIME`, ang QPU time sa segundo. Sa QPU, ang QPU time na siningil ng IBM ay nakatala sa ilalim ng `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`, ang phase kung saan tumakbo ang mga circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`\"RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU\"` is the time your jobs waited in the IBM queue. The run takes this time from the IBM job timestamps, and does not count it in `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`. If IBM does not report those timestamps for every job, the entry is absent, and the wait is part of `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`.\n"
msgstr "Ang `\"RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU\"` ay ang oras na naghintay ang mga job mo sa IBM queue. Kinukuha ng run ang oras na ito mula sa mga timestamp ng IBM job, at hindi ito binibilang sa `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"`. Kung hindi iniuulat ng IBM ang mga timestamp na iyon para sa bawat job, wala ang entry, at bahagi ng `\"RUNNING: MAPPING\"` ang paghihintay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM&reg; finishes its usage calculation some time after a job finishes. The run waits up to about a minute for it. Usage that is still being calculated after that time is not included in `QPU_TIME`, and the final usage is shown on IBM Quantum Platform. If the run cannot read the usage from IBM, `QPU_TIME` is `None`.\n"
msgstr "Tinatapos ng IBM&reg; ang pagkuwenta ng usage nito ilang sandali pagkatapos matapos ang job. Naghihintay ang run nang hanggang halos isang minuto para rito. Ang usage na kinukuwenta pa rin pagkalipas ng oras na iyon ay hindi kasama sa `QPU_TIME`, at makikita ang pinal na usage sa IBM Quantum Platform. Kung hindi mabasa ng run ang usage mula sa IBM, ang `QPU_TIME` ay `None`.\n"

