# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Function sizes {#function-sizes}"
msgstr "Mga laki ng function {#function-sizes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every job runs at one size — `S`, `M`, or `L`. If the specified size is too small, the job is rejected. If the size is larger than needed, it runs on a bigger compute profile than the work requires.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat job ay tumatakbo sa isang laki — `S`, `M`, o `L`. Kung masyadong maliit ang tinukoy na laki, tatanggihan ang job. Kung mas malaki ang laki kaysa sa kailangan, tatakbo ito sa mas malaking compute profile kaysa sa hinihingi ng gawain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The size of a Rimay job depends on the number of samples it maps: the rows of `x_train` and `x_test` for `fit-transform`, and the rows of `x_inference` for `transform`. The labels in `y_train` do not count, and a `delete` run maps no samples.\n"
msgstr "Ang laki ng isang Rimay job ay nakasalalay sa bilang ng mga sample na ima-map nito: ang mga row ng `x_train` at `x_test` para sa `fit-transform`, at ang mga row ng `x_inference` para sa `transform`. Hindi binibilang ang mga label sa `y_train`, at walang sample na ima-map ang isang `delete` run.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Size | Samples per job | Compute profile | vCPU | RAM |\n"
"| :-- | :-- | :-- | :-- | :-- |\n"
"| `S` | Up to 2,999 | `8x32` | 8 | 32 GB |\n"
"| `M` | 3,000 to 9,999 | `8x32` | 8 | 32 GB |\n"
"| `L` | 10,000 to 15,000 | `16x128` | 16 | 128 GB |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Size | Samples per job | Compute profile | vCPU | RAM |\n"
"| :-- | :-- | :-- | :-- | :-- |\n"
"| `S` | Up to 2,999 | `8x32` | 8 | 32 GB |\n"
"| `M` | 3,000 to 9,999 | `8x32` | 8 | 32 GB |\n"
"| `L` | 10,000 to 15,000 | `16x128` | 16 | 128 GB |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of samples is the only criterion. A size changes nothing but the compute profile: the [limits](#limits) on features, samples, and shots are the same for every size. `S` and `M` run on the same compute profile and differ in the number of samples each covers.\n"
msgstr "Ang bilang ng mga sample lang ang criterion. Walang binabago ang laki maliban sa compute profile: pareho para sa bawat laki ang mga [limitasyon](#limits) sa mga feature, sample, at shots. Ang `S` at `M` ay tumatakbo sa parehong compute profile at nagkakaiba sa bilang ng mga sample na sinasaklaw ng bawat isa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The default is `M`, used when a job does not request a size. A job of more than 9,999 samples must therefore request `L`.\n"
msgstr "Ang default ay `M`, na ginagamit kapag walang hiniling na laki ang job. Kaya ang job na may higit sa 9,999 sample ay dapat humiling ng `L`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also read the mapping off the function itself with `rimay.sizes_map`, and the size that a job runs at when it does not request one with `rimay.default_size`.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mo ring basahin ang mapping mula mismo sa function gamit ang `rimay.sizes_map`, at ang laki kung saan tumatakbo ang isang job kapag wala itong hiniling na laki gamit ang `rimay.default_size`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the size before submitting {#calculate-the-size-before-submitting}"
msgstr "Kuwentahin ang laki bago magsumite {#calculate-the-size-before-submitting}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run this on your own inputs. It reads them and does nothing else: no job is submitted and nothing is reserved, so you can call it as often as you like.\n"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ito sa sarili mong mga input. Binabasa lang nito ang mga ito at wala nang iba: walang isinusumiteng job at walang nirereserba, kaya maaari mo itong tawagin nang kasing dalas ng gusto mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass the data sets themselves, not their file names, in the same order as `input_file`, together with the `mode` of the run. [Step 2 of the example](#2-run-the-function) shows the call.\n"
msgstr "Ipasa ang mismong mga data set, hindi ang mga pangalan ng file, sa parehong ayos ng `input_file`, kasama ang `mode` ng run. Ipinapakita ng [Hakbang 2 ng halimbawa](#2-run-the-function) ang pagtawag.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the size is too small, the job fails with error `4600` and the message names the size to use instead. If it is larger than needed, the job runs normally and records a `4601` advisory event.\n"
msgstr "Kung masyadong maliit ang laki, babagsak ang job na may error na `4600` at ang mensahe ay nagsasaad ng laki na dapat gamitin sa halip. Kung mas malaki ito kaysa sa kailangan, normal na tatakbo ang job at magtatala ng `4601` advisory event.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example {#example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa {#example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example shows how to upload data, run the function, and retrieve the quantum-transformed features. For an end-to-end example that includes the preprocessing and the training of the classical model, see the [tutorial](/tutorials/classify-credit-risk-with-rimay-quantum-feature-extraction).\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng halimbawang ito kung paano mag-upload ng data, patakbuhin ang function, at kunin ang mga quantum-transformed feature. Para sa end-to-end na halimbawa na kasama ang preprocessing at ang pagte-train ng classical model, tingnan ang [tutorial](/tutorials/classify-credit-risk-with-rimay-quantum-feature-extraction).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Upload the data {#1-upload-the-data}"
msgstr "1. I-upload ang data {#1-upload-the-data}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example uses a small synthetic dataset with four numeric features and a binary label, so that a run needs only four qubits and finishes quickly. The next cell writes it to four CSV files: the training features, the training labels, the test features, and the features for step 4 of this example. To use your own data, write your preprocessed training and test sets to files with the same layout instead.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang halimbawang ito ng maliit na synthetic na dataset na may apat na numeric na feature at binary label, kaya apat na qubit lang ang kailangan ng run at mabilis itong natatapos. Isinusulat ito ng susunod na cell sa apat na CSV file: ang training feature, ang training label, ang test feature, at ang mga feature para sa hakbang 4 ng halimbawang ito. Para gamitin ang sarili mong data, isulat sa halip ang iyong mga preprocessed na training at test set sa mga file na may parehong layout.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the training and test files. You upload `x_inference.csv` in step 4.\n"
msgstr "I-upload ang mga training at test file. I-a-upload mo ang `x_inference.csv` sa hakbang 4.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Run the function {#2-run-the-function}"
msgstr "2. Patakbuhin ang function {#2-run-the-function}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the size of the run from the data that you uploaded, with the calculator from [Function sizes](#calculate-the-size-before-submitting).\n"
msgstr "Kuwentahin ang laki ng run mula sa data na in-upload mo, gamit ang calculator mula sa [Mga laki ng function](#calculate-the-size-before-submitting).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select a processor with at least as many qubits as your data has features, and run the function in `fit-transform` mode with that size. The sample data has four features, so any IBM Quantum processor can run it.\n"
msgstr "Pumili ng processor na may kahit kasing dami ng qubit ang bilang ng feature ng data mo, at patakbuhin ang function sa `fit-transform` mode gamit ang laking iyon. Apat ang feature ng sample data, kaya anumang IBM Quantum processor ay kayang magpatakbo nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the workload's [status](/guides/functions-get-started#check-job-status) or return [results](/guides/functions-get-started#retrieve-results) as follows:\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang [status](/guides/functions-get-started#check-job-status) ng workload o ibalik ang mga [resulta](/guides/functions-get-started#retrieve-results) tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Retrieve the results {#3-retrieve-the-results}"
msgstr "3. Kunin ang mga resulta {#3-retrieve-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download the quantum-transformed features. Pass `target_name` so that each file is saved under its own name.\n"
msgstr "I-download ang mga quantum-transformed feature. Ipasa ang `target_name` para ma-save ang bawat file sa sarili nitong pangalan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Map new data {#4-map-new-data}"
msgstr "4. I-map ang bagong data {#4-map-new-data}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After you train your model, map new data with the fitted mapping, for example to run inference. This example maps `x_inference.csv`, which the first cell of this example wrote. Pass the `mapping_id` that the fit returned, so that the new rows are mapped with the same mapping instead of a new one.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos mong i-train ang iyong model, i-map ang bagong data gamit ang na-fit na mapping, halimbawa para magpatakbo ng inference. Imamapa ng halimbawang ito ang `x_inference.csv`, na isinulat ng unang cell ng halimbawang ito. Ipasa ang `mapping_id` na ibinalik ng fit, para ang mga bagong row ay ma-map gamit ang parehong mapping sa halip na bago.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A mapping is built for the qubit layout of one processor, so pass the same `backend_name` as the fit, which the fit returned in `result[\"backend_name\"]`. Do not use `least_busy()` to choose the processor, because it might return a different one. Rimay rejects any other processor before it submits anything. The shot count also comes from the fit.\n"
msgstr "Ang mapping ay binubuo para sa qubit layout ng isang processor, kaya ipasa ang parehong `backend_name` ng fit, na ibinalik ng fit sa `result[\"backend_name\"]`. Huwag gamitin ang `least_busy()` para piliin ang processor, dahil maaari itong magbalik ng ibang processor. Tinatanggihan ng Rimay ang anumang ibang processor bago ito magsumite ng anuman. Ang bilang ng shot ay galing din sa fit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Delete a mapping {#5-delete-a-mapping}"
msgstr "5. Burahin ang mapping {#5-delete-a-mapping}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you no longer need a fitted mapping, delete it. A `delete` run does no quantum work, so it needs no processor, no shots, and no function size. You cannot undo a deletion. After deletion, the `mapping_id` no longer refers to anything, and a `transform` run with it fails.\n"
msgstr "Kapag hindi mo na kailangan ang na-fit na mapping, burahin ito. Ang `delete` run ay walang ginagawang quantum na gawain, kaya hindi nito kailangan ng processor, shots, o laki ng function. Hindi mo maaaring bawiin ang pagbura. Pagkatapos ng pagbura, wala nang tinutukoy ang `mapping_id`, at babagsak ang isang `transform` run na gumagamit nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fetch error messages {#fetch-error-messages}"
msgstr "Kunin ang mga mensahe ng error {#fetch-error-messages}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If your workload status is `ERROR`, use `job.error_message()` to fetch the error message, as follows:\n"
msgstr "Kung ang status ng workload mo ay `ERROR`, gamitin ang `job.error_message()` para kunin ang mensahe ng error, tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every error that Rimay reports carries a code from the [IBM Quantum error codes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/errors), a message, and a solution that names the value that you passed and the value that is allowed. The following table lists the most common errors:\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat error na iniuulat ng Rimay ay may kasamang code mula sa [IBM Quantum error codes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/errors), isang mensahe, at isang solusyon na nagsasaad ng value na ipinasa mo at ng value na pinapayagan. Inililista ng sumusunod na talahanayan ang mga pinakakaraniwang error:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Code | Cause |\n"
"| :-- | :-- |\n"
"| `1221` | A parameter is missing or has the wrong type, `mode` is not valid, a file named in `input_file` was not uploaded, the files do not match each other, a feature is not numeric, or the `mapping_id` does not match a stored mapping. |\n"
"| `1221` | A `\"transform\"` run names a different `backend_name` than the fit that produced its mapping. |\n"
"| `1216` | Your instance has no processor with the `backend_name` that you passed. The solution lists the processors it does have. |\n"
"| `1200` | Your API key does not have access to the instance that the job runs under. |\n"
"| `3200` | `backend_name` does not start with `ibm_`. |\n"
"| `4500` | The data has more features than the processor has qubits. |\n"
"| `6000` | The number of samples times `shots` exceeds 10 million executions. |\n"
"| `6001` | `shots` is smaller than 1. |\n"
"| `6002` | The data has more samples than a run allows. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Code | Cause |\n"
"| :-- | :-- |\n"
"| `1221` | A parameter is missing or has the wrong type, `mode` is not valid, a file named in `input_file` was not uploaded, the files do not match each other, a feature is not numeric, or the `mapping_id` does not match a stored mapping. |\n"
"| `1221` | A `\"transform\"` run names a different `backend_name` than the fit that produced its mapping. |\n"
"| `1216` | Your instance has no processor with the `backend_name` that you passed. The solution lists the processors it does have. |\n"
"| `1200` | Your API key does not have access to the instance that the job runs under. |\n"
"| `3200` | `backend_name` does not start with `ibm_`. |\n"
"| `4500` | The data has more features than the processor has qubits. |\n"
"| `6000` | The number of samples times `shots` exceeds 10 million executions. |\n"
"| `6001` | `shots` is smaller than 1. |\n"
"| `6002` | The data has more samples than a run allows. |\n"

